<header>
  <h1>Spike or Stay</h1>
  <p class="subtitle">Given an abrupt surge in public interest, will it last? Interest = Wikipedia pageviews.</p>

  <% if @replay %>
    <div class="banner replay">
      <strong>Replay as of <%= @as_of.strftime("%B %-d, %Y") %>.</strong>
      Only data from complete weeks up to <%= LiveLabel.last_complete_week_end(@as_of) %> is used.
      <%= link_to "Back to today", root_path %>
    </div>
  <% end %>
  <% if @as_of_error %><div class="banner warning"><%= @as_of_error %></div><% end %>
  <% if @source&.mode == :demo %>
    <div class="banner info">Demo mode: showing sample products (Shopify credentials not set).</div>
  <% elsif @source&.error %>
    <div class="banner error">Couldn't load products from <%= @source.shop %>: <%= @source.error %></div>
  <% elsif @source %>
    <div class="banner info">Connected to <strong><%= @source.shop %></strong>: <%= pluralize(@source.products.size, "product") %>.</div>
  <% end %>
  <% if @fatal_error %><div class="banner error"><%= @fatal_error %></div><% end %>
</header>

<% if @rows.any? %>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Product</th>
        <th>Mapped term</th>
        <th>Wikipedia article</th>
        <th>Label</th>
        <th>Confidence</th>
        <th>Reasons</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <% @rows.each do |row| %>
        <tr>
          <td>
            <% if row.products.size == 1 %>
              <%= row.products.first[:title] %>
            <% else %>
              <details>
                <summary><%= row.products.first[:title] %> <span class="count">+<%= row.products.size - 1 %> more</span></summary>
                <ul><% row.products.drop(1).each do |product| %><li><%= product[:title] %></li><% end %></ul>
              </details>
            <% end %>
          </td>
          <td>
            <%= row.mapping.term %>
            <span class="muted">(from <%= row.mapping.source %>)</span>
          </td>
          <td><%= row.article || "—" %></td>
          <% if row.error %>
            <td><span class="label label-error">Error</span></td>
            <td>—</td>
            <td class="muted"><%= row.error %></td>
          <% else %>
            <td><span class="label label-<%= row.result.label.parameterize %>"><%= row.result.label %></span></td>
            <td><%= row.result.confidence ? number_to_percentage(row.result.confidence * 100, precision: 0) : "—" %></td>
            <td>
              <%= row.result.reason %>
              <% if row.result.onset_week %><span class="muted">Surge began week of <%= row.result.onset_week %>.</span><% end %>
              <% row.notes.each do |note| %><div class="note">⚠ <%= note %></div><% end %>
            </td>
          <% end %>
        </tr>
      <% end %>
    </tbody>
  </table>
<% end %>

<footer>
  <p>
    <%# Numbers from backtest/results/step_d_results.md, analysis (a). Update if the model is retrained. %>
    Model backtested on n = <%= TrendModel.instance.trained_on["n"] %> past trends:
    leave-one-out accuracy 75% (95% CI 51–90%) vs 62% for "still rising in week 6".
    The difference is within noise at this sample size. Confidence is the model's probability, not a guarantee.
  </p>
  <p>Gradual trends never trigger a 3x surge, so they show as "No surge detected".
    Try a replay: <%= link_to "?as_of=2017-06-12", root_path(as_of: "2017-06-12") %> (fidget spinners) or
    <%= link_to "?as_of=2025-01-27", root_path(as_of: "2025-01-27") %> (Labubu, Dubai chocolate).
    Replays of trends the model was trained on are in-sample, so they demo the pipeline rather than prove accuracy.</p>
</footer>
